        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(msteams): add timeouts to file consent upload requests",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nTeams file consent uploads validated the SharePoint consent URL, then performed the upload PUT without a request deadline. If the upload request never completed, the accepted file delivery path could remain pending indefinitely.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nAdd a bounded consent upload timeout using the existing timer timeout resolver, and keep the abort timer active until the upload request finishes. The upload deadline is transfer-aware: it keeps a 5 minute base stall bound, then adds size-derived transfer budget so valid large SharePoint uploads are not cut off by a fixed 5 minute ceiling. The SSRF host/IP validation and upload headers/body semantics are unchanged.\n\n## User Impact\n\nWhen a Teams file consent upload stalls, OpenClaw now aborts the request instead of waiting forever, so the file delivery flow can fail quickly and surface the error path. Large valid file-consent uploads get additional budget based on payload size instead of sharing the same fixed deadline as a small upload.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs extensions/msteams/src/file-consent.test.ts extensions/msteams/src/request-timeout.test.ts` passed: 68 tests.\n- `node_modules/.bin/oxfmt --check extensions/msteams/src/request-timeout.ts extensions/msteams/src/file-consent.ts extensions/msteams/src/file-consent.test.ts extensions/msteams/src/request-timeout.test.ts` passed.\n- `node_modules/.bin/oxlint --tsconfig config/tsconfig/oxlint.extensions.json extensions/msteams/src/request-timeout.ts extensions/msteams/src/file-consent.ts extensions/msteams/src/file-consent.test.ts extensions/msteams/src/request-timeout.test.ts` passed.\n- `git diff --check` passed.\n- Transfer-aware proof: `resolveMSTeamsSharePointUploadTimeoutMs(100 * 1024 * 1024)` now resolves to 700000ms: 300000ms base plus 400000ms transfer budget at 256KiB/s.\n- Controlled upload-path proof: a 512KiB file-consent upload completed at 301000ms, after the old fixed 300000ms cutoff but before the size-derived deadline; the fetch signal remained un-aborted and the upload resolved.\n- Stall proof retained: a controlled stalled consent upload aborts through `AbortSignal` and throws `MS Teams file consent upload timed out after 25ms`.\n- Not run: live Microsoft Teams tenant / real SharePoint upload.\n",
        "branch": "alix/msteams-file-consent-upload-timeouts",
